{{define "applet-style-hive"}}
## Style: match Hive

Make this look like part of Hive Desktop. The page cannot import Hive's components or
Tailwind, so write plain CSS against these rules.

- **Colour:** use only the `--hv-*` variables, so every theme works, light ones included. Cool neutrals, with amber (`--hv-accent`) as the only warm hue. Accent marks what is selected or primary, never decoration. Severity colours carry meaning only.
- **Surfaces:** `--hv-app` for the page, `--hv-sidebar` or `--hv-pane` for sidebars and side panes, `--hv-raised` for dialogs, `--hv-chip` for chips and badges. Separate regions with a 1px `--hv-border` line rather than a shadow or a gap.
- **Text:** `--hv-text` for primary, `--hv-text-2` for secondary, `--hv-text-3` for labels and hints, `--hv-text-4` for the faintest.
- **Type:** sans for prose and mono for ids, paths, keys and numbers: `'Inter Variable', Inter, -apple-system, system-ui, sans-serif` and `'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace`. Sizes in px: 10.5, 11.5, 12.5, 13.5, 15, 17, and 28 only for a large figure. Body is 13 to 13.5. Weights stay at 400, 500 and 600.
- **Section headers:** mono, 10.5px, weight 600, `0.12em` tracking, uppercase, `--hv-text-3`.
- **Shape:** radii of 4, 6 and 8px, and 11px for a large panel. Dialogs may have a soft shadow. Nothing else does. No gradients.
- **Density:** one-line rows of 26 to 32px, with secondary detail in a tooltip or a detail pane rather than a second line. Header bars around 44 to 48px, footers around 30px.
- **Sidebars:** a fixed width around 240px on `--hv-sidebar`, with a 1px border on the inner edge. Rows are one line with a bare leading glyph in a fixed 16px cell. Trailing controls appear on hover in a reserved column, so hovering never moves a name. Children are not indented and have no connector lines. Mark the open item with accent text and medium weight, or `--hv-selection` with a 2px accent rail on its left edge, never both. Only one item is marked at a time.
- **Lists:** the selected row gets `--hv-selection` or `--hv-accent-tint`, the hovered row `--hv-row-hover`.
- **Controls:** buttons at 24 to 28px tall. Icons are Lucide, as inline SVG at 14px with stroke width 2. Icon-only buttons need a `title`.
- **States:** every list has an empty state, and failures show their real message inline, in `--hv-severity-error`. A long action shows that it is busy.
- **Keyboard:** everything can be done from the keyboard, and the keys are shown in a footer hint bar using small `<kbd>` chips. Escape backs out of one thing at a time.
- **Words:** sentence case, short and plain. No marketing copy, no emoji.
{{end}}
{{define "applet-style-named"}}
## Style: {{.Reference}}
{{if eq .Reference "terminal"}}
A terminal: monospace everywhere, a dark background with one or two phosphor colours, box-drawing borders, a block cursor, no rounded corners and no images. Everything works from the keyboard.
{{else if eq .Reference "editorial"}}
Editorial: like a well-set magazine. A serif display face, a strong type hierarchy, an off-white page, thin rules instead of boxes, and one restrained accent colour.
{{else if eq .Reference "swiss"}}
Swiss: a strict grid, one grotesque sans in a few sizes, flush-left text, black and white with a single saturated accent, and no decoration of any kind.
{{else if eq .Reference "brutalist"}}
Brutalist: raw and loud. Thick black borders, hard offset shadows, system fonts at big sizes, clashing flat colours, and visible structure.
{{else if eq .Reference "arcade"}}
Arcade: a retro game cabinet. Neon on near-black, a pixel font, scanlines, chunky buttons, and bouncy motion and sound.
{{end}}
{{end}}
